      listing: "Listing", payouts: "Payouts", compliance: "Compliance",
      faq1q: "I already list on another site. Can I list here too?", faq1a: "Yes. Injishi is not exclusive: list wherever you like, and keep control of your calendar and rates.",
      faq2q: "What kind of accommodation can I list?", faq2a: "Hotels, motels, tented camps, guest houses, apartments, lodges and villas anywhere in Rwanda. Bars, restaurants, coffee shops and residences let on a lease can register too. If you can show you are entitled to run or let the place, it qualifies. Other businesses can join the Private Sector Federation through its own page.",
      faq3q: "How long until my listing is live?", faq3a: "Once your review is done and your documents and photos are approved, your listing goes live.",
      faq4q: "Do I have to accept every booking?", faq4a: "No. Set your availability, minimum stay and house rules. You can close dates at any time without penalty.",
      faq5q: "What does Injishi charge the host?", faq5a: "Two charges, and no commission: a one-time registration fee, shown before you pay, and a monthly plan that starts once your listing is live. You receive the rate you set.",
      faq6q: "When am I paid?", faq6a: "The guest's payment is held in escrow and paid out after check-in. Before your listing goes live, we confirm how and when payouts reach you by mobile money or bank.",
      faq7q: "What happens if a guest disputes a stay?", faq7a: "Our team reviews the issue before money moves. The payment remains in escrow while we do, so neither side has to chase the other for a refund.",
